From 7cf4279b444b2a0afca94c5da9d1da293f20f719 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:07:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drm/apple: Open the HDR and EDR paths on the firmware 27
 panel, opt-in

Every HDR path in the driver is keyed to the desktop 26.x firmware: the
connector's Colorspace, HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA and PQ_REFERENCE_LUMINANCE
(apple_connector_attach_hdr() through dcp_fw_compat_is_desktop()), the
PQ colour element at a mode set (dcp_hdr_output_supported()), PQ content
shown as EDR (dcp_panel_edr_supported()), the panel's peak luminance
(A128, res_max_panel_brightness()), the ADT EDR ceiling and the EDR swap
fields. A firmware 27 panel (the J716s XDR panel, DCP 27.3) runs the
same IOMFB template and gets none of it: its connector has no colour
properties at all.

Two opt-ins. appledrm.fw27_panel_hdr=1 gives the panel the connector
properties, lets a PQ commit select the timing's PQ element when the
firmware lists one and tag RGB surfaces BT.2020 PQ, reads the peak
luminance (A128) and the ADT headroom ceiling, and when the peak comes
back adds the HDR static metadata block to the synthesised EDID.
appledrm.fw27_panel_edr=1 (runtime) adds what the desktop 26.x panel
does with PQ content: brightness x headroom, display EDR scale and the
headroom used, carried in the present's swap record at the desktop
offsets (+0x358 flags, +0x376 limit, +0x37e scale, +0x3e6 headroom,
all within bytes the firmware 27 record left reserved; the 27.3 wire
layout moves them with its gaps). Firmware 27 has not been seen to take
those fields: this is the experiment.

The EDR step logic leaves dcp_edr_prepare() for dcp_edr_plan(), shared
by the desktop swap and the firmware 27 present; the binary64 helpers
move to dcp-edr.h. Without the parameters nothing changes: the desktop
path keeps its values, firmware 27 sends what it sent.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
